From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: lib: bootm: fix unsafe wdt_overflow append to bootargs

boot_prep_linux() appends " wdt_overflow=<n>" by strcat-ing directly
onto the pointer returned by env_get("bootargs"). This is broken in
both bootargs states:

- bootargs unset: env_get() returns NULL and strcat(NULL, ...) raises
  a synchronous abort. Unset bootargs is a legitimate state - it is
  how a signed FIT DTB's /chosen/bootargs is allowed to survive
  fdt_chosen(), so any verified-boot flow that carries the command
  line in the signed devicetree crashes at bootm.
- bootargs set: the strcats write up to ~26 bytes past the end of the
  env hashtable's malloc'd value string. Corruption detonates later
  in the boot path whenever bootargs is not the most recent heap
  allocation; observed on RZ/V2L as an abort after "Starting kernel"
  with " wdt_overflow=0" ASCII bytes in the fault registers.

Build the amended command line in a properly sized buffer and store it
back with env_set(), skipping the append when bootargs is unset (the
signed-DTB case, where injecting anything would defeat the design).

Reported-at: https://github.com/renesas-rz/renesas-u-boot-cip/issues/3
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-fable-5
---
 arch/arm/lib/bootm.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm/lib/bootm.c
+++ b/arch/arm/lib/bootm.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <asm/cache.h>
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WDT
+#include <malloc.h>
 #include <wdt.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -205,8 +206,25 @@
 	char *commandline = env_get("bootargs");
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WDT
-	strcat(commandline, " wdt_overflow=");
-	strcat(commandline, simple_itoa(watchdog_overflow));
+	/*
+	 * Append the watchdog-overflow status without writing into the
+	 * env-owned string: strcat on the env_get() pointer overruns its
+	 * allocation, and bootargs may legitimately be unset (a signed FIT
+	 * DTB carrying /chosen/bootargs relies on that to survive
+	 * fdt_chosen()), in which case there is nothing to append to.
+	 */
+	if (commandline) {
+		size_t cmdline_len = strlen(commandline) + 32;
+		char *buf = malloc(cmdline_len);
+
+		if (buf) {
+			snprintf(buf, cmdline_len, "%s wdt_overflow=%s",
+				 commandline, simple_itoa(watchdog_overflow));
+			env_set("bootargs", buf);
+			free(buf);
+			commandline = env_get("bootargs");
+		}
+	}
 #endif
 
 	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(OF_LIBFDT) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_LMB) && images->ft_len) {
